<title>FRANCE: Bouygues, Lyonnaise may link in telecoms - Le Monde.</title>
<headline>Bouygues, Lyonnaise may link in telecoms - Le Monde.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Bouygues and Lyonnaise des Eaux are considering an alliance in telecommunications and could strike a deal in the coming weeks, French afternoon daily Le Monde said on Friday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted sources at Bouygues Telecom as saying: &quot;Following the failure with SNCF (railways), we're working to find alternatives&quot; and quoted Lyonnaise Cable chairman Cyrille Peloux as saying only, &quot;I cannot say anything&quot;.</p>
<p>The newspaper noted that the groups were seeking a strategy in the wake of recent agreements between Cie Generale des Eaux and Havas.</p>
</text>
